Some of the steps in computerising an existing manual system include: systems analysis, systems design, programming, testing, changeover to the new system, operation and maintenance.

The changeover to the new system from the manual system can be achieved in three ways:
(a) Immediate change;
(b) Running the manual and computerised systems in parallel;
(c) Gradually introducing the new system a subsystem at a time.

For each of the changeover techniques above, state an application which is most appropriate.
